+# Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct
+
+## Our Pledge
+
+We as members, contributors, and maintainers pledge to make participation in our
+community a harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of experience
+level, background, identity, or personal characteristics.
+
+We are committed to fostering an open, welcoming, respectful, and collaborative
+environment.
+
+## Our Standards
+
+Examples of behavior that contributes to a positive environment include:
+
+- Being respectful and constructive in discussions.
+- Welcoming different viewpoints and experiences.
+- Giving and accepting constructive feedback.
+- Focusing on what is best for the project and its community.
+- Showing empathy toward other community members.
+- Respecting the privacy and security principles of the project.
+
+Examples of unacceptable behavior include:
+
+- Harassment, discrimination, or personal attacks.
+- Trolling, insulting, or deliberately disruptive comments.
+- Publishing another person's private information without permission.
+- Sharing sensitive data, credentials, personal health data, or other confidential information.
+- Misrepresenting the project's capabilities or security guarantees.
+- Any other conduct that could reasonably be considered inappropriate in a
+  professional and collaborative environment.
+
+## Enforcement Responsibilities
+
+Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing our standards
+of acceptable behavior.
+
+Maintainers may remove, edit, or reject comments, commits, code, issues, pull
+requests, or other contributions that do not align with this Code of Conduct.
+
+## Scope
+
+This Code of Conduct applies within all project spaces, including GitHub issues,
+pull requests, discussions, community communication channels, and public
+representation of the project.
+
+## Reporting Issues
+
+If you experience or witness unacceptable behavior, please report it privately
+to the project maintainers.
+
+Please do not post sensitive reports, personal information, credentials, or
+private data publicly in GitHub issues.
+
+## Enforcement
+
+Maintainers may take appropriate action, including warnings, requests to remove
+content, temporary restrictions, or permanent removal from the community.
+
+## Attribution
+
+This Code of Conduct is adapted from the Contributor Covenant, version 2.1.
